# Task Credential Manifest

Lists, per credential this repo's tasks need, where an agent finds it — an
env var name, an owner-store file path, or a provisioned-file path. Never a
value. Safe to commit: every row below is a placeholder.

| Purpose | Reference | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| Example: deploy to staging | env var `CLOUD_DEPLOY_TOKEN` | read via `$CLOUD_DEPLOY_TOKEN` in-process; never print, commit, or quote in issue/PR text |
| Example: SSH access to `<host>` | provisioned file: `~/.ssh/<repo>_deploy` | used by `ssh -i <path>`; public half installed on `<host>`, private half never leaves the owner's machine |
| Example: `<service>` API key | owner-store path `~/.config/<tool>/<file>` | read in-session to authenticate; report readiness/outcome only |

Delete the example rows and add one row per real credential. If a task needs
a credential not listed here, that is a **missing-credential** case per
`.loom/docs/credentials.md` — ask the operator for the name, shape, and
provisioning path only, never the value, then add the resulting row here.
